{"title":"Antlion","html":"<article class=\"wp\"><div class=\"wp-main\"><p class=\"wp-lede\">A level 19 Antlion that attacks with slash (melee).</p>\n      <h2>Fighting it</h2><div class=\"s\"><i>Weak</i> <span class=\"tag-chip weak\">crush</span><span class=\"tag-chip weak\">burn</span> &nbsp; <i>Resists</i> <span class=\"tag-chip resist\">stab</span></div>\n      <p class=\"s muted\">A weakness adds 30% damage and a resistance takes 30% off (the game's own rule).</p>\n      \n      \n      \n      <h2>Levels</h2><div class=\"q-picker\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Level\"><a class=\"q-chip\" href=\"#/monster/antlion\">All levels</a><a class=\"q-chip\" href=\"#/monster/antlion?lv=18\">Lv 18 <span>51</span></a><a class=\"q-chip\" href=\"#/monster/antlion?lv=19\">Lv 19 <span>44</span></a><a class=\"q-chip\" href=\"#/monster/antlion?lv=20\">Lv 20 <span>4</span></a><a class=\"q-chip on\" href=\"#/monster/antlion?lv=21\">Lv 21 <span>4</span></a><a class=\"q-chip\" href=\"#/monster/antlion?lv=22\">Lv 22 <span>2</span></a></div>\n      <p class=\"s muted\">The same monster spawns at different levels, and its hitpoints, damage and XP follow its level (the game’s own formula). In the game a monster more than 5 levels above you shows its level as “???”.</p>\n      <div class=\"g-scroll\"><table class=\"g-table q-table\"><thead><tr><th>Level</th><th>HP</th><th>Damage</th><th>XP</th><th>Elite (HP · dmg · XP)</th><th>Seen</th><th>Mostly</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class=\"\" data-href=\"#/monster/antlion?lv=18\" title=\"Pick level 18\"><td><b>18</b></td><td>57</td><td>14.4</td><td>900</td><td class=\"muted\">171 · 20.2 · 2,700</td><td>51</td><td>near <a href=\"#/map/place/Colossus%20Ruins\">Colossus Ruins</a></td></tr><tr class=\"\" data-href=\"#/monster/antlion?lv=19\" title=\"Pick level 19\"><td><b>19</b> <span class=\"muted\">(base)</span></td><td>61</td><td>15</td><td>950</td><td class=\"muted\">183 · 21 · 2,850</td><td>44</td><td>near <a href=\"#/map/place/Colossus%20Ruins\